{"html":"<div>\n<h2 id=\"x-series-firmware-upgrade-file\"> <strong>X Series </strong>Firmware Upgrade File</h2>\n<h3 id=\"controllermainboard-firmware-upgrade-file\"> Controller(mainboard) Firmware Upgrade File</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li>Old: <a href=\"https://www.1laser.com/pages/firmware-updates\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">[Download Mainboard Firmware 1.0]</a></li>\n  <li>New: <a href=\"https://www.1laser.com/pages/firmware-updates\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">[Download Mainboard Firmware 2.0]</a></li>\n</ul><div>\n\n</div><h3 id=\"hmipanel-upgrade-file\"> HMI(panel) Upgrade File</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li>Old: <a href=\"https://www.1laser.com/pages/firmware-updates\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">[Download Control Panel Firmware 1.0]</a></li>\n  <li>New: <a href=\"https://www.1laser.com/pages/firmware-updates\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">[Download Control Panel Firmware 2.0]</a></li>\n</ul><div>\n\n</div><p><a href=\"#/wiki/firmware-update\"><strong>How to Select the Correct Firmware Upgrade File</strong></a></p>\n<div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"firmware-upgrade-guide-for-x-series-users\"> Firmware Upgrade Guide (For X Series Users)</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yQOyZdQbYLM&amp;t=48s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">X Series Firmware Upgrade Video Tutorial</a></li>\n</ul><div>\n\n</div><h3 id=\"h-1-updating-control-board-firmware\"> 1. Updating Control Board Firmware</h3>\n<h4 id=\"h-11-updating-control-board-firmware-via-rdwords-only-for-windows-users\"> 1.1 Updating Control Board Firmware via RDwords (Only For Windows Users)</h4><div>\n\n</div><p>1.Install the RDWorks program on your computer.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"RDWorks install screen\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"RDWorks setup wizard\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"RDWorks main interface\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>2.Connect the device to the computer using a data cable and start RDWorks.</p>\n<p>3.Click &quot;System Setting&quot; - &quot;Controller&quot; to enter the controller upgrade interface.Enter &quot;rd8888&quot; in the &quot;Vendor password&quot; input field and click the &quot;Input&quot; button to confirm the password.</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片10.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"RDWorks system setting menu\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片11.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"RDWorks vendor password field\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>4.Click &quot;Upgrade firmware&quot;. In the pop-up window, find and select the corresponding motherboard firmware upgrade file, wait and confirm that the upgrade is complete.</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片12.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Select mainboard firmware file\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade/图片13.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Firmware upgrade progress window\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>5.Click &quot;OK&quot; to close the prompt window. Restart the device.</p><div>\n\n</div><p><strong>Caution:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Be sure to select an upgrade file that matches the controller. (You can check the bar code label on the motherboard to determine whether it is new or old. The old motherboard number has &quot;1G&quot; and the new motherboard does not.)</strong></li>\n</ul><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片16.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Mainboard barcode label closeup\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片17.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Old controller board example\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片18.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"New controller board example\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><ul>\n  <li>Cannot upgrade compared to the lower upgrade file of the current controller.</li>\n  <li>Restart the device after the upgrade.</li>\n</ul><div>\n\n</div><h4 id=\"h-12-updating-control-board-firmware-via-makerboost\"> 1.2 Updating Control Board Firmware via MakerBoost</h4>\n<p>(Panel firmware upgrade support will be added in a future update)</p><div>\n\n</div><p>1.Launch MakerBoost and click &quot;Switch&quot; to connect to the XRF/XT machine.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片19.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"MakerBoost device list screen\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片20.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"MakerBoost connected to X Series\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>2.Open &quot;Settings&quot;, select &quot;Vendor Setting&quot;, and enter the password: TL9501.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片21.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"MakerBoost vendor settings menu\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片22.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"MakerBoost firmware upgrade option\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>3.After clicking &quot;System&quot;, select &quot;Firmware Upgrade&quot;. Upload the corresponding device firmware file. Wait for the upgrade process to complete. Power off the device completely, then restart it to finalize the controller firmware upgrade.</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片23.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Firmware upload dialog in MakerBoost\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片24.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Firmware upgrade success message\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p><strong>Caution:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>MUST select a firmware file EXACTLY matching your controller model.(The selection method is the same as mentioned above)</strong></li>\n  <li>NEVER attempt to downgrade (e.g. installing firmware older than the current version).</li>\n  <li>During the controller firmware upgrade process, do <strong>NOT</strong> power off the device, disconnect the computer from the device, or press any buttons on the equipment.</li>\n</ul><div>\n\n</div><h3 id=\"h-2-updating-panel-firmware-via-tf-card\"> 2. Updating Panel Firmware via TF Card</h3><div>\n\n</div><p>1.Use a blank TF card, a card reader, and a docking station to connect the TF card to your computer. </p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片25.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"TF card and card reader\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>2.Open “Disk Utility” and format the TF card to ensure the file system is FAT32.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片26.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Disk Utility formatting TF card\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片27.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"TF card format confirmation\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>3.Extract the front panel firmware upgrade files to the root directory of the TF card. Then safely eject the TF card from your Mac and remove it.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片28.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Copy panel firmware to TF card\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片29.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"TF card root folder with firmware\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/图片30.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Ejecting TF card safely\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/firmware-upgrade-3/图片31.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"TF card removed from computer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>4.Ensure the device is powered off completely. Remove the right-side protective cover of the control panel, then insert the TF card into the TF card slot at the bottom of the control panel.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/firmware-upgrade-3/图片32.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Inserting TF card into panel slot\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/firmware-upgrade-3/图片33.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Panel detecting TF card firmware\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>5. Power on the device. The front panel will automatically begin updating. When the screen displays “SD CARD PROCESS...END!”, the upgrade is complete. Power off the device, remove the TF card, and then power it on again to finalize the upgrade.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/firmware-upgrade-3/图片34.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Panel showing firmware update progress\">\n</figure>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/firmware-upgrade-2/firmware-upgrade-3/图片35.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"SD CARD PROCESS END message\">\n</figure>\n</div>","toc":[{"id":"x-series-firmware-upgrade-file","level":2,"text":"X Series Firmware Upgrade File"},{"id":"controllermainboard-firmware-upgrade-file","level":3,"text":"Controller(mainboard) Firmware Upgrade File"},{"id":"hmipanel-upgrade-file","level":3,"text":"HMI(panel) Upgrade File"},{"id":"firmware-upgrade-guide-for-x-series-users","level":2,"text":"Firmware Upgrade Guide (For X Series Users)"},{"id":"h-1-updating-control-board-firmware","level":3,"text":"1. Updating Control Board Firmware"},{"id":"h-2-updating-panel-firmware-via-tf-card","level":3,"text":"2. Updating Panel Firmware via TF Card"}]}